  (b) Any paid employee, officer, director, agent, or contractor of RECF (or
      its affiliates) when acting within the scope of their employment,
      official duties, or contract.

  Clarification: Independent, unpaid tournament volunteers, Head Referees,
  educators, students, and local Event Partners acting in a personal, team, or
  independent local-event capacity are NOT Excluded Entities solely because
  they participate in or volunteer at an RECF-affiliated event.

"Commercial Purpose" means any use, copying, modification, hosting, or
distribution primarily intended for or directed toward commercial advantage,
business revenue, or private monetary compensation, including but not limited to:
  (a) Selling, licensing, renting, leasing, or charging any fee for access to
      the Software or any modified version ("Fork");
  (b) Operating a paid, subscription-based, or ad-monetized hosted service or
      SaaS offering based on the Software;
  (c) Publishing a monetized or paid app-store listing derived from the
      Software; or
  (d) Integrating or using the Software inside a for-profit business or paid
      commercial product or service.

"Permitted Community Use" means personal, educational, research, or
non-commercial community use of the Software (including running a local LAN or
self-hosted sync server at a tournament), provided that:
  (a) No fee is charged specifically for access to, distribution of, or hosting
      of the Software or Fork; and
  (b) The activity is not for a Commercial Purpose and is not carried out by or
      on behalf of an Excluded Entity.
  Standard tournament entry or venue registration fees collected by a school,
  club, or independent Event Partner to run a robotics competition do not by
  themselves make volunteer use of the Software a Commercial Purpose.

